## Noise Reduction

The original detection evaluated:

```text
All Event ID 4624 successful authentication events
```

The tuned detection evaluates:

```text
Event ID 4624
AND
Logon Type 3
AND
Non-local source address
```

This reduces the volume of unrelated successful authentication presented to the analyst.

Exact baseline and tuned counts were not retained in the tuning record and are therefore not represented as measured values.

---

## Detection Engineering Lesson

TUNE-001 demonstrated an important detection-engineering principle:

> Detection logic and detection names should reflect what the available telemetry can actually prove.

A network logon may be consistent with SMB activity, but Event ID 4624 with Logon Type 3 alone does not establish that an administrative SMB share was accessed.

The revised detection therefore reports the observable behavior:

```text
Suspicious Remote Network Logon
```

rather than asserting administrative SMB activity without sufficient supporting telemetry.

